---
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';

const socials = [
  { href: SITE.links.youtube, label: 'YouTube' },
  { href: SITE.links.instagram, label: 'Instagram' },
  { href: SITE.links.whatsapp, label: 'WhatsApp' },
].filter((link) => link.href.length > 0);

/**
 * Licensing footnote. The reasoning lives in docs/adr/0010; only what constrains
 * this file is repeated here.
 *
 * The repository link is the AGPL-3.0 section 13 offer of Corresponding Source. It sits in the
 * shared footer so a fork inherits the mechanism instead of having to remember it. A fork repoints
 * SITE.repository — never the two licence URLs, which must keep pointing at the licence texts.
 *
 * Wording is load-bearing and was corrected in review, so do not "tidy" it:
 * - section 13 obliges an offer to the users of THAT instance, not publication to the world, so
 *   "oferecer o código a quem usar" is correct where "deixar público" would overstate it.
 * - CC BY-NC-SA has three conditions. Dropping ShareAlike understates the licence and misleads a
 *   reuser about what adapting the worksheets actually requires.
 *
 * rel="noreferrer" only. noopener is inert without target="_blank", and nothing here opens a new
 * context. noreferrer is NOT redundant with the Referrer-Policy header: that header still sends the
 * origin cross-origin, whereas noreferrer sends nothing.
 *
 * data-pagefind-ignore is belt-and-braces — data-pagefind-body already scopes indexing to lesson
 * bodies, but this text repeats on every route, so it would pollute results if that ever moved.
 */
const AGPL_URL = 'https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html';
const CC_URL = 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/deed.pt-BR';

const linkClass = 'text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2';
---

<footer class="mt-16 border-t border-ink-100 bg-surface-alt">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-8 text-sm text-ink-700">
    <p class="font-semibold text-ink-900">{SITE.name}</p>
    <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose">{SITE.description}</p>

    {
      socials.length > 0 && (
        <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
          {socials.map((link) => (
            <li>
              <a class={linkClass} href={link.href}>
                {link.label}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      )
    }

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-ink-500">
      Seu progresso fica salvo apenas neste aparelho. Não pedimos cadastro e não guardamos seus
      dados em nenhum servidor.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-ink-500" data-licence data-pagefind-ignore>
      O código deste site é público no <a class={linkClass} href={SITE.repository} rel="noreferrer"
        >GitHub</a
      >, sob a licença <a class={linkClass} href={AGPL_URL} rel="noreferrer">AGPL-3.0</a> — quem publicar
      uma versão modificada precisa oferecer o código dela a quem usar. As aulas e as fichas estão sob
      a licença <a class={linkClass} href={CC_URL} rel="noreferrer">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>: você pode
      imprimir, compartilhar e adaptar, desde que dê crédito, não use para fins comerciais e
      mantenha a mesma licença.
    </p>
  </div>
</footer>
